## Interface: 11509
## Title: Pathwise
## Notes: Follows your character's progression and tells you what to do next.
## Author: noelagnelius
## X-Curse-Project-ID: 1767676
## Version: 0.52.0
## OptionalDeps: QuestieDB
## X-License: GPL-3.0-or-later
## SavedVariables: PathwiseDB
## SavedVariablesPerCharacter: PathwiseCharDB

# Interface numbers: 11509 = Classic Era 1.15.9 (verified in game
# 2026-10-22 with /dump select(4, GetBuildInfo()) - re-check after each
# patch); 16001 = WoW Forever 1.60.1 (the client's internal name is Camelot).
#
# Four TOCs, all loading the same files; only the interface line differs:
#   Pathwise_Vanilla.toc  11509         Classic Era
#   Pathwise_Forever.toc  16001         WoW Forever
#   Pathwise_Camelot.toc  16001         WoW Forever, if it looks for that suffix
#   Pathwise.toc          11509, 16001  fallback for clients that pick up neither
# Platform_Forever.lua does nothing outside WoW Forever. tests/run.lua checks
# that the four stay in step.

# Load order matters:
#  0. Libs        - LibStub, LibTameable-1.0 (Classic Era data only)
#  1. Locales     - string table (Pathwise.L)
#  2. Platform    - the only layer that calls flavor-specific WoW API
#  3. Core/Init   - namespace, saved variables, events, callbacks, commands
#  4. Data        - plain Lua tables for this flavor
#  5. Core        - logic modules (never call WoW API directly)
#  6. Classes     - class modules (they check the class themselves)
#  7. Integrations- optional data from other addons (QuestieDB)
#  8. UI          - frames, popups, slash command binding

